<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Musabba'at sultanate</h1><p class="st-meta">1650 CE – 1785 CE (approx.) · capital Bara</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Fur-linked sultanate in Kordofan, rival of the Funj and Darfur, that briefly dominated the plains between the Nile and Darfur.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Musabba'at were a branch of the ruling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/keira-dynasty">Keira</a> family of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darfur-sultanate">Darfur</a> who moved east into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kordofan">Kordofan</a> in the 17th century after a dynastic dispute. They founded a sultanate in the plains of northern and central Kordofan, around Bara.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kordofan">Kordofan</a> was a contested frontier rich in gum, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> and slaves, crossed by routes between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darfur-sultanate">Darfur</a>. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Hashim in the later 18th century, the Musabba'at expanded their rule over much of Kordofan, competing with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/funj-sultanate">Funj Sultanate</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/darfur-sultanate">Darfur Sultanate</a>. Little is known of their institutions.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1785 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-tayrab">Muhammad Tayrab</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darfur-sultanate">Darfur</a> invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kordofan">Kordofan</a> and drove Hashim out, ending the Musabba'at state. Kordofan stayed under Darfur until the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/turco-egyptian-sudan">Turco-Egyptian Sudan</a> conquered it in 1821.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="sultanate, 1650 CE – 1785 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">sultanate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:92.54%;width:2.69%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1650 CE – 1785 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>sultanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bara</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Hashim</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Fur, Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/sudan">Sudan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Musabba'at, Kordofan sultanate</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1718&amp;focus=musabbaat-sultanate" aria-label="Musabba'at sultanate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5350 1697 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Musabba'at sultanate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5670 1953L5695 1926"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5695 1926h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5670 1953h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5670 1953h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Bara. <a href="/atlas?year=1718&amp;focus=musabbaat-sultanate">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

